WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.360
With Justice League smashing onto our screens,
DC is upping the stakes with an epic, bust-'em-up

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.620
brawl featuring the heavyweights of the comic
book line-up.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.300
But life wasn't always teamwork and spandex
for the cast of Justice League.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.420
In our universe, there was a time when Flash
sang opera, Aquaman studied marine biology,

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.400
and Batman grew up just outside of Boston
… with parents.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:21.880
Ben Affleck

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.320
Ben Affleck took his first acting role at
the age of 7, and he acted regularly from

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.280
that first role all the way through his teens,
despite moving with his family often.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.860
When the Affleck clan finally settled down
in Massachusetts, 8-year-old Ben Affleck became

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.659
friends with an older kid who lived two blocks
away in the same neighborhood: Matt Damon,

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.399
who he's still friends with today.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.100
"Or you could learn about things that are
actually true, like how incredibly short Matt

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.740
Damon is."

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.020
"Or the fact that Ben's left eye twitches
every time you say the word Gigli."

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.920
They were both interested in acting, and Ben
Affleck still credits Matt Damon and their

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:55.140
childhood friendship as the reason he decided
to become a "real" actor.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.660
These days, he's obviously looking a little
older, which is exactly what the new Batman

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:00.660
needed to be.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.030
"This guy, he's like.. he's is older... he's
really f----- up and he's really broken down.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.240
And he's on the edge of moral bankruptcy.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.080
I'm clearly your man!"]

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:10.740
Jason Momoa

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.700
Most people were probably introduced to Jason
Momoa as Khal Drogo, but the Hawaiian-born

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.660
actor has gained acclaim for more than his
role in Game of Thrones.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.280
Before leading the Dothraki, Momoa traveled
the galaxy as the dreadlocked Ronon Dex in

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:27.810
Stargate: Atlantis and destroyed hordes of
magical monsters in the 2011 remake of Conan

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.520
the Barbarian.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:31.440
And it's safe to say that he's changed a lot
over the years.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.079
Momoa originally went to school to study marine
biology, an education which may come in handy

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.400
now that he's donning the scaled armor of
Aquaman.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.440
Plans are also in development for a standalone
Aquaman film to be released in 2018.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:44.920
Gal Gadot

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.360
The decision to cast Gal Gadot as Wonder Woman
seemed to come out of left field for a lot

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.640
of people, but the Israeli-born model definitely
has the background to pull off a superpowered

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.140
heroine.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:59.460
Gadot grew up in Israel and was crowned Miss
Israel in 2004 before spending her next two

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.460
years in the Israeli Defense Forces.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.759
"You were trained in the Israeli Army."

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.009
" Yeah, that's probably where it all began."

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.320
"I was a girl scout."

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:12.250
Gadot went on to star in four Fast &amp; Furious
films, then immediately transitioned to the

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.600
DC film universe as our favorite Amazon warrior
princess.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:19.700
She claims that when she auditioned for Batman
v Superman, she didn't know she was trying

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.700
out for Wonder Woman.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:25.120
All she knew was that it was a Zack Snyder
film, and her first guess was that it was

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.120
an audition for a new Catwoman.

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:30.680
Judging by her standalone film's ratings,
Gadot seems to be shaping up to be a solid

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.400
Wonder Woman for the 21st century.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:33.820
Ezra Miller

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:38.760
Born in Wyckoff, a small town in northern
New Jersey, Ezra Miller grew up in a family

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.140
that was all about the arts.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.760
A lot of that must have rubbed off on the
young boy, who first sang on stage at the

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.920
age of 6 and went on to study at the New York
Metropolitan Opera.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.700
In 2008, the 16-year-old starred in his debut
film, Afterschool, but the movie that brought

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:56.200
Ezra Miller into the public eye was definitely
2011's We Need to Talk About Kevin.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.100
He's since starred in Fantastic Beasts and
Where to Find Them, and it's looking like

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.240
he's got a long run as the Flash ahead of
him.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.020
Amy Adams

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.780
Amy Adams never wanted to be an actress as
a child—she wanted to be a dancer.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.200
But even that dream wasn't entirely likely.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.040
When she was 18, she found herself working
at Hooters just to pay for a car.

00:03:14.049 --> 00:03:16.550
"You used to be a Hooters waitress, which
I can see… why."

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.550
"As you can see.."

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.960
I'd be proud of that, I'd be like, 'I had
the body people.'"

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.920
By chance, she happened to be in Minnesota
in 1999 when a casting crew came through looking

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.820
to fill parts in the Kirsten Dunst film Drop
Dead Gorgeous.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.480
She nailed the audition and snagged her first
film role in the process.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:36.780
Amy Adams' first major role was as Leonardo
DiCaprio's love interest in 2002's Catch Me

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:41.319
If You Can, directed by Steven Spielberg,
but her breakout hit didn't come until 2007,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.540
when she starred in Disney's Enchanted.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.880
Since then, Amy Adams has been nominated for
five Oscars, won two Golden Globes, and moved

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.900
well past the status of "rising" star.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.560
And somehow that smile hasn't changed a bit
since high school.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.140
Ray Fisher

00:03:56.740 --> 00:04:00.840
Born and raised in New Jersey, Ray Fisher
started acting early in high school musicals,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.260
but he only applied to drama school on a bet.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.819
To his surprise, he was accepted, and he's
since worked mostly with the Shakespeare Theatre

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.320
of New Jersey.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.620
In 2013, he played Muhammad Ali in the off-Broadway
show "Fetch Clay, Make Man," a role which

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:16.320
finally caught the attention of Hollywood.

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:21.460
Except for his brief cameo in Batman v Superman,
Justice League will be Ray Fisher's first

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:21.960
film.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.460
Fisher has definitely shown his skills on
stage, and hopefully he'll bring the same

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.140
enthusiasm to the role of Cyborg.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:32.400
He's already slated to star in a standalone
Cyborg film, rumored to be coming out in 2020.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.360
And after Justice League, there's no doubt
that the 29-year-old will be getting more

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.340
movie offers than ever.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:38.960
Henry Cavill

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:43.440
Believe it or not, Man of Steel wasn't Henry
Cavill's first time in blue spandex and a

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:43.940
red cape.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:49.440
He was originally cast as Superman in 2006's
Superman Returns, but due to a director change

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:52.800
and subsequent recasting, Cavill lost the
role to Brandon Routh.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:57.700
According to MTV, Cavill had gone so far into
the casting process that he'd even tried on

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:58.420
the Supes cape.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:02.420
The DC universe seemed determined to keep
Cavill out, but he finally got his chance

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.480
to fly with 2013's Man of Steel.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:09.840
Now, Cavill has finally pushed his way into
pop culture as the modern face of Clark Kent.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.820
It must feel good after so many near-hits:
in addition to missing out on Superman Returns,

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:19.960
Cavill almost became James Bond and was Stephanie
Meyers' first choice for Edward in Twilight,

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.200
although that was probably more of a near-miss
for Cavill.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:23.880
Thanks for watching!

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.400
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.820
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

